{"id":275,"date":"2016-05-16T12:50:28","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:50:28","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/badminton-super-series-maybank-malaysia-open-2012-announcement\/"},"modified":"2016-08-31T17:36:04","modified_gmt":"2016-08-31T17:36:04","slug":"maybank-malaysia-open-2012-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/maybank-malaysia-open-2012.html","title":{"rendered":"Badminton Super Series: MAYBANK Malaysia Open 2012 Announcement"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float:left;\">\n<\/div>\n<p>The Malaysia Open has always been the first badminton super series tournament of the year.<\/p>\n<p>This year in 2012, the <strong>MAYBANK Malaysia Open 2012<\/strong> will be hosted in the capital city of Malaysia, <em>Kuala Lumpur<\/em>.<\/p>\n<p>It will be at the National Sports Complex, Bukit Jalil, from <em>10-15 January 2012<\/em>.<\/p>\n<p>This year is exceptional because the badminton <strong>Malaysia Open 2012<\/strong> will be the SECOND Super Series event of the year.<\/p>\n<p>The first Super Series event held in the year will be the Victor Korea Open 2012 from 3-8 January 2012. The slight difference was that it was a Super Series PREMIER event.<\/p>\n<p>The Malaysia Open is one of the most prestigious badminton tournaments in the world. It was held since 1937 and had become a Super Series event since 2007.<\/p>\n<p>Today, the Malaysian Super Series attracts the world&#8217;s BEST badminton players to compete in Malaysia.<\/p>\n<p>Badminton has been a very popular sport in Malaysia. Malaysians would definitely account for most of the crowd.<\/p>\n<p>The event venue, <em>Putra Stadium<\/em>, has a seating capacity of 12,000.<\/p>\n<p>I believe it is expecting an 80% occupancy rate.<\/p>\n<h2>Preliminary Highlights<\/h2>\n<h3>Men&#8217;s Singles<\/h3>\n<p>Malaysian badminton fans will definitely be there to support their local hero: home favourite singles player Lee Chong Wei.<\/p>\n<p>Lee is eyeing his 8th Malaysia open gold medal in this 2012 tournament.<\/p>\n<p>The current world no.1 Lee Chong Wei is a 7-times champion at the Malaysian Open in the past 8 occasions.<\/p>\n<p>Apart from the Malaysian crowd, there usually are smaller groups of overseas spectators supporting their own country.<\/p>\n<p>The crowd will also be there to watch the &#8216;<em>4 kings of badminton<\/em>&#8216; [including Chong Wei], <strong>Lin Dan, Peter Gade, and Taufik Hidayat<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<h3>Men&#8217;s Doubles<\/h3>\n<p>Crowd pullers in the men doubles category are the former world no.1 <strong>Koo Kien Keat and Tan Boon Heong<\/strong> of Malaysia.<\/p>\n<p>The Malaysian pair is on a dry spell, they had not won a tournament title in 2011.<\/p>\n<p>Will the pair start regain their momentum towards regaining their world no.1 status by winning their first gold medal of the year at the Maybank Malaysia Open 2012?<\/p>\n<p>Even on home ground, it won&#8217;t be an easy task for the Malaysians.<\/p>\n<p>They will be up against the likes of <strong>Jung Jae Sung and Lee Yong Dae<\/strong> from Korea and defending champions from China, <strong>Chai Biao and Guo Zhendong<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>They might even meet the 2008 Olympics Gold Medalists <strong>Markis Kido and Hendra Setiawan<\/strong> of Indonesia.<\/p>\n<p>Koo and Tan stand a good chance to reach to the finals of the tournament because the current world no.1 men doubles <strong>Cai Yun and Fu Hai Feng<\/strong> will not be present.<\/p>\n<p>2011 Super Series Final winner and all England Champion, <strong>Mathias Boe and Carsten Mogensen<\/strong> will also not be present.<\/p>\n<h3>Women&#8217;s Category<\/h3>\n<p>Other crowd pullers include young and talented women singles player from India, <strong>Saina Nehwal<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>The Chinese have been dominant in badminton.<\/p>\n<p>But can Saina Nehwal start the year strong by beating the top Chinese women singles players, <strong>Wang Yi Han, Wang Xin,<\/strong> and <strong>Wang Shi Xian<\/strong> to prevent a possible China v China in the women singles final?<\/p>\n<h3>Mixed Doubles<\/h3>\n<p>People will also be there to see extremely entertaining mixed doubles pair from Denmark, Joachim Fischer and Christinna Pedersen who has been performing very well lately.<\/p>\n<h3>Don&#8217;t Miss It!<\/h3>\n<p>It will truly be a tough battlefield for badminton players around the world.<\/p>\n<p>Just in case you didn&#8217;t know, there is an exciting badminton drama since the inception of the OSIM BWF events in 2011 and the drama goes on in this very Malaysian Super Series 2012.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"maybank-malaysia-badminton-open-2012-event-program.html\" onclick=\"return FIX.track(this);\">Click here to read on the EVENT PROGRAM for the Maybank Malaysia Open 2012<\/a> and I will give you a brief introduction on the OSIM BWF badminton drama.<\/p>\n<p>Finally, here is a video showing you the highlight of the 2011 Malaysian Super Series.<\/p>\n<p\/><iframe loading=\"lazy\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/lXfxav8WJUA\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"><\/iframe><\/p>\n<p>Feel the atmosphere and be part of the event!<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.maybankbadmintonopen.com\/ticketing.htm\" target=\"_blank\" onclick=\"return FIX.track(this);\">Get more information on the tickets and <strong>buy it HERE!<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>The price of the ticket for the tournament is reasonably low to ensure all badminton fans in the country have a chance to attend.<\/p>\n<h3>Latest Updates!<\/h3>\n<h4>DAY 1 Update<\/h4>\n<p><a href=\"maybank-malaysia-open-2012-qualifying-rounds.html\" onclick=\"return FIX.track(this);\">Maybank Malaysia Open 2012 Qualifying Rounds Wrap Up<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"maybank-malaysia-open-2012-special-events.html\" onclick=\"return FIX.track(this);\">Check out the Special Events Organized by Maybank!<\/a><\/p>\n<h4>DAY 2 Update<\/h4>\n<p><a href=